(6253199, 924298, 96751, '<td valign="top">Such an odd perspective!!!!  Exceptional lighting and detail.  So weird and wonderful.</td>', 'Such an odd perspective!!!!  Exceptional lighting and detail.  So weird and wonderful.', '2010-12-13 21:21:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253201, 924723, 96751, '<td valign="top">This is officially my final five countdown towards my 10,000th comment.  It suddenly acquired enormous portent for me, so I chose the final five from the thumbnails.  This is number 9,997.<br/> <br/>Simple yet effective.  I love that ceiling and the fan blur, but the oblique angle really adds a sense of daydreaming.  I imagine that I am on vacation in a tropical setting, and don''t want to get out of bed yet.</td>', 'This is officially my final five countdown towards my 10,000th comment.  It suddenly acquired enormous portent for me, so I chose the final five from the thumbnails.  This is number 9,997. Simple yet effective.  I love that ceiling and the fan blur, but the oblique angle really adds a sense of daydreaming.  I imagine that I am on vacation in a tropical setting, and don''t want to get out of bed yet.', '2010-12-13 21:22:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253202, 924886, 61084, '<td valign="top">Subject is out of focus, too centered and quite honestly not that interesting in the context of the photo. The trees are disappearing on the top left and full of "jaggies" Also, the photo has a severe color cast and is very flat. The whites are much bluer than they should be. When shooting in snow try using a +1 Ev exposure compensation to get the exposure correct. Also, sorry to say I don''t feel this has a "from the ground up" feel to it.<br/> <br/>Not trying to be too hard here. I''m trying to give you some constructive advice so please take it as that. :)<br/> <br/>Not voting until later in the week.</td>', 'Subject is out of focus, too centered and quite honestly not that interesting in the context of the photo. The trees are disappearing on the top left and full of "jaggies" Also, the photo has a severe color cast and is very flat. The whites are much bluer than they should be. When shooting in snow try using a +1 Ev exposure compensation to get the exposure correct. Also, sorry to say I don''t feel this has a "from the ground up" feel to it. Not trying to be too hard here. I''m trying to give you some constructive advice so please take it as that. :) Not voting until later in the week.', '2010-12-13 21:22:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253203, 924393, 96751, '<td valign="top">So very good and odd.  A great combination for me.  Love the dramatic lighting and crusty, rusty detail in the foreground, and the smooth but scratched plane that separates the pipe for the dreamy sky.  The intriguing squiggle provokes all sorts of guesses.</td>', 'So very good and odd.  A great combination for me.  Love the dramatic lighting and crusty, rusty detail in the foreground, and the smooth but scratched plane that separates the pipe for the dreamy sky.  The intriguing squiggle provokes all sorts of guesses.', '2010-12-13 21:24:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253208, 924852, 61084, '<td valign="top">I really like the idea and obvious effort put into this. However the composition is a too centered for me both vertically and horizontally. I think this would have been more effective as a landscape with a slight wider angle. You could have still gotten everything into the frame and composed it a little better. Just my opinion. I do like how it''s shot to be from the perspective of the person in the grave though and would keep that same idea.<br/> <br/>Not voting until later in the week.</td>', 'I really like the idea and obvious effort put into this. However the composition is a too centered for me both vertically and horizontally. I think this would have been more effective as a landscape with a slight wider angle. You could have still gotten everything into the frame and composed it a little better. Just my opinion. I do like how it''s shot to be from the perspective of the person in the grave though and would keep that same idea. Not voting until later in the week.', '2010-12-13 21:26:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253209, 924784, 96751, '<td valign="top">Awesome processing</td>', 'Awesome processing', '2010-12-13 21:26:48.000000', NULL, 1),
