(6253218, 924876, 61084, '<td valign="top">Love the perspective of the building and windows washers. That''s really great. I also love the reflection of the adjacent building and the blue tones here.<br/> <br/>What I don''t like and can easily be avoided in processing is the haloing around the top of the buildings and the overall exposure is a bit flat and needs just a little more punch with a curves adjustment to really make it pop. Overall I think it''s a great shot. Nice eye.<br/> <br/>Not voting until later in the week.</td>', 'Love the perspective of the building and windows washers. That''s really great. I also love the reflection of the adjacent building and the blue tones here. What I don''t like and can easily be avoided in processing is the haloing around the top of the buildings and the overall exposure is a bit flat and needs just a little more punch with a curves adjustment to really make it pop. Overall I think it''s a great shot. Nice eye. Not voting until later in the week.', '2010-12-13 21:32:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253220, 924746, 96751, '<td valign="top">Interesting lines.</td>', 'Interesting lines.', '2010-12-13 21:33:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253221, 924600, 96751, '<td valign="top">This is officially my final five countdown towards my 10,000th comment.  It suddenly acquired enormous portent for me, so I chose the final five from the thumbnails.  This is number 9,996.<br/> <br/>I am very familiar with this installation, and have wanted to shoot it for quite some time now.  In fact, this is the pov that I have wanted to shoot, so thanks a lot.  I''m going out on a limb here and guessing that this is by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=90098" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mgarsteck</a>, as he''s a local, and the editing reminds me of his work.  If this is NOT Matt, consider it a compliment.  <br/> <br/>I really like this image for all its lines (real and implied), and the exceptional editing to maintain all the tonal ranges.  There is a lot of movement, especially considering how fixed these lights are, and I feel as though I''m zooming through space, or that time is zooming towards me.</td>', 'This is officially my final five countdown towards my 10,000th comment.  It suddenly acquired enormous portent for me, so I chose the final five from the thumbnails.  This is number 9,996. I am very familiar with this installation, and have wanted to shoot it for quite some time now.  In fact, this is the pov that I have wanted to shoot, so thanks a lot.  I''m going out on a limb here and guessing that this is by  mgarsteck, as he''s a local, and the editing reminds me of his work.  If this is NOT Matt, consider it a compliment.   I really like this image for all its lines (real and implied), and the exceptional editing to maintain all the tonal ranges.  There is a lot of movement, especially considering how fixed these lights are, and I feel as though I''m zooming through space, or that time is zooming towards me.', '2010-12-13 21:34:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253222, 924639, 61084, '<td valign="top">Out of focus in parts, Too centered and sorry to say not very interesting overall...sorry.<br/> <br/>Not voting until later in the week.</td>', 'Out of focus in parts, Too centered and sorry to say not very interesting overall...sorry. Not voting until later in the week.', '2010-12-13 21:34:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253223, 924439, 96751, '<td valign="top">This is officially my final five countdown towards my 10,000th comment.  It suddenly acquired enormous portent for me, so I chose the final five from the thumbnails.  <br/> <br/>This is number 10,000.  Congratulations.<br/> <br/>I don''t know why, but I adore this image.  The unusual pov and odd "expression" are certainly part of it, but it is also a highly artistic image, in spite of having a "pet" in it.  I can''t help but feel this by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous</a> because it reminds me of this image:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=410572" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_410572.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_410572.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_410572.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Of course, who shot this is not as important as how wonderful it is.  The pp''ing is so perfectly suited to the intent of the image, and I can hear this pooch''s Machiavellian laughter echoing across the heaths.  The tiny black clouds just above the trees on the left reminds me of crows - whose presence is always considered an ominous portent.  Although there is none shown, I imagine a thin fog hugging the ground, and the air damp and chilled.  Fabulous.  Front page for me.</td>', 'This is officially my final five countdown towards my 10,000th comment.  It suddenly acquired enormous portent for me, so I chose the final five from the thumbnails.   This is number 10,000.  Congratulations. I don''t know why, but I adore this image.  The unusual pov and odd "expression" are certainly part of it, but it is also a highly artistic image, in spite of having a "pet" in it.  I can''t help but feel this by  posthumous because it reminds me of this image:   Of course, who shot this is not as important as how wonderful it is.  The pp''ing is so perfectly suited to the intent of the image, and I can hear this pooch''s Machiavellian laughter echoing across the heaths.  The tiny black clouds just above the trees on the left reminds me of crows - whose presence is always considered an ominous portent.  Although there is none shown, I imagine a thin fog hugging the ground, and the air damp and chilled.  Fabulous.  Front page for me.', '2010-12-13 21:35:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6253224, 924826, 96751, '<td valign="top">dreamy</td>', 'dreamy', '2010-12-13 21:35:56.000000', NULL, 1),
